## UI/UX Principles

### Visual Hierarchy

- One primary focal point per section
- Use size, weight, and color for importance
- Primary actions visually dominant

### Accessibility

- WCAG AA contrast
- Focus rings: `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring`
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44px
- Semantic HTML: `button`, `label`, `fieldset`

### Content Density

- Avoid overcrowding
- Cards: one primary idea per card
- Tables: 4–7 columns typically

### Error & Loading States

- Use `text-destructive` for errors
- Use `FieldError` for form validation
- Provide loading feedback for async actions

**Full-screen loading:** When a route or section shows a loading state that replaces the main content (e.g. `if (isLoading) return ...`), use the `Loading` component from `@/components/ui/loading`. Do not use inline `Loader2` or custom spinners for this pattern.

```tsx
// ✅ Good: full-screen loading
if (isLoading) {
  return <Loading className="min-h-0 flex-1" />; // flex child: fills available space
}
// or
if (isLoading) {
  return <Loading />; // page-level: uses default min-h-screen
}

// ❌ Bad: custom spinner for full-screen loading
if (isLoading) {
  return (
    <div className="flex min-h-0 flex-1 items-center justify-center">
      <Loader2 className="h-8 w-8 animate-spin text-muted-foreground" />
    </div>
  );
}
```

Use `Loader2` or similar only for **inline** loading (e.g. inside a button, small section).

### Responsive

- Sidebar: 256px fixed; collapse to icon-only on mobile (if implemented)
- Content: `flex-1` to fill
- Use `min-h-0` on flex children that scroll

